-- title:
--   The coefficients of the explicit function $H_\star$ (Theorem 5.1)
-- statement:
--   The explicit function $H_\star$ of Theorem 5.1 is the member of the family $\mathcal H$ (Definition 5.2) determined by the 3,150 rational coefficients stored in the data file of §C.1 of Mo–Cheng–Ding (reproducibility archive [MCD26], file `data/coefficients.json`). The level is $U_0=79742997/50000000=1.59485994$.
--
--   The stored coefficients are:
--
--   1. $V_{ijl}$ for one index pair from each orbit $\{(i,j),(11-i,11-j)\}$, namely the pairs with $i\le5$ (72 orbits, 35 coefficients each);
--   2. $R_{ijl}$ for one pair from each orbit $\{(i,j),(5-i,5-j)\}$ with $6i+j\le17$, except the corner orbits, on which $R=0$ (16 orbits);
--   3. all $B_l$ and $D_l$, $0\le l\le34$.
--
--   The remaining coefficients are reconstructed from (5.3):
--
--   $$
--   V_{11-i,11-j,l}=-V_{ijl},\qquad R_{5-i,5-j,l}=R_{ijl},\qquad R_{ijl}=0\ \text{ for }(i,j)\in\{0,5\}^2 .
--   $$
--
--   Then $H_\star=\mathrm{familyH}(V,R,B,D)$, i.e. formula (5.2) for $\gamma\ge0$, extended to $\gamma<0$ by $H(\gamma,\varphi,\theta,\psi)=H(-\gamma,-\varphi,\theta,-\psi)$.
--
--   This is the object whose conditions (H0)–(H4) at level $U_0$ constitute Theorem 5.1.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The rows are stored as lists of rationals, copied verbatim from the archive; `hstarV`, `hstarR`, `hstarB`, `hstarD` read them with the orbit reconstruction above.
-- source:
--   Mo, Cheng, Ding, arXiv:2609.07979v6, Theorem 5.1 (p.30), Definition 5.2 (pp.31–32), §C.1 Table 6 (pp.55–56); data: Mo, Cheng, Ding, Delaunay stretch-factor upper bound: reproducibility supplement, Zenodo doi:10.5281/zenodo.23835635, data/coefficients.json

